  "id": "ostrobothnian_menuett_polska",
  "name": "Menuett och polska (Finland-Swedish Ostrobothnian fiddle dance)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Fiddle dance music of the Swedish-speaking communities of Ostrobothnia in western Finland, where the minuet, long gone from most of Europe, survived as a living folk dance alongside the polska, notably in Jeppo near Nykarleby. Otto Andersson's folk-music collection at Åbo Akademi documents it from the early twentieth century, Svenskt visarkiv later recorded fiddlers in Swedish-speaking Finland and Åland, and the minuet tradition of the Swedish-speaking areas is listed in the Finnish National Inventory of Living Heritage.",
  "recipe": "classic early-1940s menuett och polska, improv On Frame, string improv branch. fiddle. field recording. small-diaphragm pencil condenser, portable field-recorder pre. tape 15ips.",
